// error
// #5258/#6112: `[]` type-checks fine on its own (`checkSliceLit`), but an
// EMPTY slice literal with no declared type to check against has no element
// to infer its own concrete type from -- `checkSliceLit` answers invalid (0),
// and `vDefaultInferredTypeInvalid` (validatefuncdecl.bit) is what turns
// that into E0159, the same "no type to infer" diagnostic a bare `x = nil`
// gets (fn_default_arg_inferred_untyped.bit). No longer "not a literal" --
// #6112 removed that rule entirely -- but this default still has nothing to
// give the parameter.

fn g(x = []) {}

fn main() {
  g()
}
